---
import KickoffSession from "../../components/KickoffSession.astro";

const photos = [
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5410.jpg",
        alt: "Yulia Korobkova speaking beside the podium. Her name is on the slide.",
        caption: "On data centres as a high-tech industrial campus.",
    },
];
---

<KickoffSession
    documentTitle="A campus, not an isolated building. | Canada2080"
    description="Yulia Korobkova on data-centre design and Canadian compute capacity at the Canada2080 kickoff."
    eyebrow="Capacity · 1:55 p.m."
    headline="A campus, not an isolated building."
    name="Yulia Korobkova"
    bio="Yulia Korobkova is Data Centers Studio Leader and Vice President at Corgan in Toronto. Her practice combines architecture, project leadership, and the delivery of compute infrastructure."
    profileUrl="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yulia-korobkova/"
    podiumSrc="/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5410.jpg"
    podiumAlt="Yulia Korobkova speaking beside the podium. Her name is on the slide."
    photos={photos}
>
    <p class="lede">
        Canada, she said, already has the land, the people, the technology, and
        the manufacturing base.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            She compared a modern data centre with light industry. She did not
            compare Canada with the United States.
        </li>
        <li>
            Closed-loop cooling, she said, uses about as much water as an
            office. Noise is lower than an Amazon distribution centre.
            Contamination is almost nothing, lower than a bottling plant.
        </li>
        <li>
            The shift she named is away from isolated buildings and toward a
            high-tech industrial campus, with buffers, local jobs, and the
            community in the plan.
        </li>
        <li>
            The barrier she named is the real-estate habit that still prefers
            the isolated building. Change that, and the campuses can be built
            here.
        </li>
    </ul>
</KickoffSession>
